SEC. S-26.111. SIGNS.

(a) Nothing in this division shall be construed to regulate the display of government signs.

(b) Except as provided in Subsections (c) and (d) below, signs must comply with the provisions for business zoning districts contained in Article VII.

(c) In addition to the maximum number of signs permitted on the Property pursuant to the regulations contained in Article VII, one flag or banner may be erected on the Property for each 20 feet, or fraction thereof, of frontage on a right-of-way.

(d) No flag or banner may:

(1) be within 10 feet of another flag or banner;

(2) have an effective area of more than 20 square feet;

(3) hang lower than nine feet above grade;

(4) hang higher than 20 feet above grade; or

(5) project more than 24 inches into the right-of-way. (Ord. Nos. 23422; 25267)

